stance in clear cell carcinoma of the ovary</article-title><source>Oncology</source><year>2002</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>353</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Oncology||62|349||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12138243</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Joseph</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Kernick</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Othumpangat</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lei</surname><given-names>YX</given-names></name><name><surname>Yuan</surname><given-names>BZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ong</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expression profile of eukaryotic translation factors in human cancer tissues and cell lines</article-title><source>Mol Carcinogen</source><year>2004</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>179</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Carcinogen||40|171||bib10|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knudsen</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Frydenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name><name><surname>Leffers</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tissue-dependent variation in the expression of elongation factor-1 alpha isoforms: isolation and characterisation of a cDNA encoding a novel variant of human elongation-factor 1 alpha</article-title><source>Eur J Biochem</source><year>1993</year><volume>215</volume><fpage>549</fpage><lpage>554</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Biochem||215|549||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8354261</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Francoeur</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tissue-specific expression in mammalian brain, heart, and muscle of S1, a member of the elongation factor-1 alpha gene family</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1992</year><volume>267</volume><fpage>24064</fpage><lpage>24068</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||267|24064||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1385435</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lund</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Knudsen</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Vissing</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Tommerup</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assignment of human elongation factor 1alpha genes: EEF1A maps to chromosome 6q14 and EEF1A2 to 20q13.3</article-title><source>Genomics</source><year>1996</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>359</fpage><lpage>361</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Genomics||36|359||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8812466</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newbery</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillingwater</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Dharmasaroja</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wharton</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ribchester</surname><given-names>RR</given-name